From 46ee0576e5a0addf9707445040d2bf344dd150a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:43:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/10] media: platform: add the Hi3798MV100 VDH decoder core
 with H.264

Add the driver for the VDH block of Hi3798MV100 set-top-box SoCs. It is
a V4L2 stateless memory-to-memory decoder: userspace parses the
bitstream and submits picture and slice parameters through request
controls, the driver programs the descriptor tables the engine reads,
and the engine writes 16x16-tiled NV21 frames.

This patch carries the framework around the engine -- the device, the
videobuf2 queues, the interrupt-driven job loop and the table area --
plus the H.264 backend, the codec the block was brought up on. The table
area is programmed once at probe, so it takes HEVC's read-only CABAC
table with it even though that codec arrives in a later patch. The
driver lands in its final layout: the parts that do not depend on which
block is underneath -- media node registration, buffer handling, the
common context lifecycle -- live in histb_vdec_core.c and the v2
generation keeps its own files.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
